{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-categorical-fourier-exists-harmonic","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:categorical-fourier-exists-harmonic","kind":"remark","title":"Projections and harmonic analysis on $A$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-fourier"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-fourier-exists","tags":["fourier","peter-weyl","harmonic-analysis"],"text":"categorical-fourier-transform-exists-harmonic.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:categorical-fourier-exists-harmonic\"></a><p>Concretely, given the family of irreducible representations (irreps), the Fourier transform provides a family of projections, each isolating the component of an endomorphism on a given irrep. This structural existence theorem underpins the harmonic analysis on the categorical Frobenius–Hopf algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-fourier-transform-exists-harmonic.md","heading":"Remark","number":"4.21.15","page":"b/rem-categorical-fourier-exists-harmonic","qa":{"counts":{"pass":43,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":1,"notPassing":1}}}
